\ tools/dict-dump-addr.4 - dict-dump.4, but each line carries the
\ ADDRESS as well as the value, so call targets can be resolved.
\
\ Emits, for every word in the dictionary:
\     N <body-start> <body-end> <name>
\     B <addr> <value>          (one per body cell)
\
\ tools/dict-dump.4 prints sizes only, which is enough to census
\ opcode frequency but not enough to follow a call: a call cell holds
\ a RELATIVE offset, so the target is addr + CELL + value and cannot
\ be computed without knowing addr. Added in Iteration 156 for
\ tools/encoding-census.py.
\
\ Usage (4-byte cells, with the shell loaded so the census covers it):
\   printf 'S" pool.4" INCLUDED\nS" locals.4" INCLUDED\nS" shell.4" INCLUDED\nS" tools/dict-dump-addr.4" INCLUDED\nBYE\n' \
\     | ./relf32 kernel32.img | tr -d '\\r' > dump.txt

BASE @ DECIMAL
VARIABLE PREVLINK
VARIABLE NFA
VARIABLE LNK
VARIABLE GO
VARIABLE BP
VARIABLE BE
: CELLB 1 CELLS ;
: DUMP
  HERE PREVLINK !
  FORTH-WORDLIST @ NFA !
  -1 GO !
  BEGIN GO @ WHILE
    NFA @ DUP C@ 31 AND 1+ ALIGNED + BP !
    PREVLINK @ BE !
    \ The raw count byte carries flag bits above the length - bit 5 is
    \ the MACRO flag cross.4's PRIMITIVE sets. TYPE below masks them
    \ off, so without this line an image rebuilt from this dump would
    \ silently lose every flag.
    S" H " TYPE NFA @ . NFA @ C@ . CR
    S" N " TYPE BP @ . BE @ . NFA @ 1+ NFA @ C@ 31 AND TYPE CR
    BEGIN BP @ BE @ < WHILE
      ." B " BP @ . BP @ @ . CR
      BP @ CELLB + BP !
    REPEAT
    NFA @ CELLB - DUP PREVLINK ! @ LNK !
    LNK @ 0= IF 0 GO ! ELSE PREVLINK @ LNK @ + NFA ! THEN
  REPEAT ;
\ The S line anchors every address above to an offset in the saved
\ image, which runs from START to HERE. Without it the layout pass
\ cannot tell where the pre-dictionary prologue begins. Printed before
\ DUMP runs, so HERE is the value the dump itself will see.
\ `."` is compile-only in this kernel and prints nothing at the
\ interpreter, so the label goes through S" ... " TYPE instead. That
\ cost a silent empty anchor line once.
S" S " TYPE START @ . HERE . CR
DUMP
\ The prologue: the cells between START and the oldest word's link
\ cell. ip = base starts executing at offset 0, so the first two are
\ code and the image cannot be rebuilt without them. DUMP walks bodies
\ only and never sees this region.
\
\ This MUST be a definition. A DO/+LOOP typed at the interpreter runs
\ once and stops - the same interpret-mode hazard GOALS.md records for
\ IF/THEN in this kernel. It printed one line and looked like a dump
\ with a short prologue rather than like a broken loop.
: PROLOGUE-DUMP
  START @ DUP 6 CELLS + SWAP DO
    S" P " TYPE I . I @ . CR
  1 CELLS +LOOP ;
PROLOGUE-DUMP
BASE ! BYE
